' DESIGN RULES / REQUIRED CONSTRAINTS (proposal, implement after approval)
' 1) One team registration per edition/team code. Exactly ONE LEADER per team (partial unique index on team_members when role=LEADER).
' 2) Team capacity configured per hackathon_editions; INITIAL min=4, max=4, default=4 INCLUDING LEADER. Admin may change per edition.
' 3) One edition/domain mapping per pair; only enabled domains accepted. Initial seed has exactly the 12 user-provided domains.
' 4) One published form version per edition. Changes create a NEW form version; already submitted teams retain original version and answers.
' 5) Admin can edit ALL questions incl required: wording, choices, order, help, input, validation, conditional visibility. Core fields nullable in DB if made optional.
' 6) Q25 IS BOOLEAN investor_pitch_interest; YES/NO. Q20-Q24 and Q26 are only relevant when YES. Do not require hidden/inapplicable questions.
' 7) Q18 count derived from team_members; Q19 names derived from other team_members; Q17 leader/member from role; do not maintain redundant strings.
' 8) Canonical team/member identity columns support lookup; answers provide a form-version-specific history of displayed questions, including derived/bound values as snapshots.
' 9) Initial payment form requires transaction_id AND proof screenshot when payment enabled; admin config controls required flags. Submit != paid; claims start PENDING.
' 10) Enforce one VERIFIED non-refunded payment per team; allow another attempt after REJECTED proof. Verify transaction uniqueness where provider permits.
' 11) Revenue = SUM(verified claimed_amount) - SUM(recorded refunds), not unverified claims; full refunds flagged in reporting.
' 12) Images/documents stored in Supabase Storage; database stores metadata + stable paths and optional URL. Sensitive images in private buckets (short-lived signed URLs).
' 13) Supabase Auth owns admin passwords/sessions; admin_users.auth_user_id references auth.users.id. Only APPROVED admins login. Only SUPER_ADMIN can approve.
' 14) Q30 terms acceptance must be TRUE; Q31/Q32 require an explicit answer but FALSE is allowed. Consent decisions attributed per team member and policy version.
' 15) Client disables SUBMIT until configured required fields validate; backend repeats validation atomically (published form, capacity, configured payment fields, duplicates).
' 16) Admin dashboard filters apply to data retrieval AND exports; XLSX header purple #8C52FF, frozen first row, Autofilter, tailored widths, wraps, typed columns.
' 17) SUPER_ADMIN has full access; ADMIN is restricted to individually assigned permissions. Payment/finance/admin security remain SUPER_ADMIN only.
' 18) RLS/private storage, restricted exports, immutable audit trails, signed file access, server-side validation and payment-verification permissions required.
' 19) Core 24 tables created by migrations 01-05; four new permission/CMS tables are PROPOSED in migration 07 (not applied remotely).

' 20) CMS slot revisions enable Draft -> Private Preview -> Review -> SUPER_ADMIN Publish, without changing public theme/layout.
' 21) Media files remain in Supabase Storage; public website never references private registration/payment assets.
@enduml
